steps.instruction:
In the IDE, select Tools > Board > Arduino/Genuino UNO. Paste the following code (using digital pin 5):
```
int ledPin = 5;
void setup(){ pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT); }
void loop(){ digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH); delay(8.3); digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW); delay(8.3); }
```
Click the “check” icon to compile, select the correct COM port (e.g., COM5), then click the “upload” icon to transfer the code to the board.

Replace the loop with a constant‑on command:
```
int ledPin = 5;
void setup(){ pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT); }
void loop(){ digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH); }
```
Compile and upload as above.
